# Everything under data/ is produced by running the pipeline, and it is not small - one 81 minute match is
# hundreds of megabytes:
#
#   cache/      the audio track of each recording as wav (250 MB for one match), so a rescan need not re-decode it
#   segments/   Stage A's per-frame results, chunk by chunk, and the scrub proxies built from them
#   matches/    one directory per match: events, tags, reports, replays, preview clips and exported reels
#   games/      the combined multi-clip game video's manifest and its low-resolution marking proxy
#   videos/     local input footage (see the .gitignore in there)
#   models/     downloaded detector weights and saved calibrations (see the .gitignore in there)
#
# All of it can be rebuilt from the source video, so none of it is committed. Small hand-written inputs that live
# here - a saved calibration, a set of landmark annotations - are ignored too; force-add one if it is worth
# keeping, for example:
#
#   git add -f data/models/calibration_half_a.json
*
!.gitignore
